;; LE-22: two operands whose shapes cannot be broadcast raise a located,
;; catchable shape error — they do not read out of bounds and do not crash.
;;
;;   (* (vector 1 2 3) (vector 4 5))
;;     before  #(4 10 4.4e-323), exit 0 — the element-wise kernel looped to
;;             operand 1's length over operand 2's array, so the last element
;;             is whatever followed the vector in the arena
;;     after   input.esk:16:29: Shape mismatch in tensor-mul: shapes (3) and
;;             (2) are not broadcast-compatible, exit 1
;;
;; The tensor spelling of the same pair was worse: the runtime's -1
;; "not broadcastable" verdict was discarded, the uninitialised result rank was
;; read back, and the program died with a fatal signal.
(display "before")
(newline)
(display (* (vector 1 2 3) (vector 4 5)))
(display "MUST-NOT-PRINT")
(newline)
